{
    "background_story": "Lana grew up in a traditional household where conventionality was highly valued. Her parents, both respected members of their community, expected her to follow in their footsteps. Lana obediently pursued a career in law, just like her father, and married a man from a good family, just as her mother had done. She settled into a comfortable suburban life, complete with a white picket fence and two children. Lana's days were filled with PTA meetings, charity events, and dinner parties, all carefully curated to maintain a perfect facade. However, beneath the surface, Lana yearned for something more. She secretly painted and wrote poetry, but kept these creative pursuits hidden, afraid to disrupt the carefully constructed conventionality of her life. As she approached middle age, Lana began to wonder if she had sacrificed too much of herself to fit into the mold of societal expectations.",
